  "result": "Perfect! All tests pass. The vulnerability has been fixed with two changes:\n\n1. **Fixed `findIssueById` in src/server/repositories/issue-repository.ts** - Added `orgPredicate` filter to enforce organization scope at the database level, preventing queries from returning issues belonging to other organizations.\n\n2. **Added defense-in-depth check in `getIssue` in src/server/services/issue-service.ts** - Added `assertOrgScope(actor, issue.orgId)` after fetching the issue to verify it belongs to the expected organization, even if the repository layer somehow returns an unexpected result.\n\nThe root cause was that `findIssueById` was not filtering by organization - it only queried by issue ID. This allowed an authenticated user to retrieve any issue in the database by knowing its ID, bypassing the organization boundary. The fixes ensure organization scope is enforced at both the database query level and the service layer.",
